WEBVTT

1
00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:34.958
<b>Arjuna's second question</b>
<b>about an enlightened being was</b>

2
00:00:34.958 --> 00:00:37.166
<b>"How does such a person speak?</b>

3
00:00:37.166 --> 00:00:42.916
<b>In other words, how does </b>
<b>he react to life's events?"</b>

4
00:00:42.916 --> 00:00:47.041
<b>The following verses, including this one, </b>
<b>answer these questions.</b>

5
00:00:47.041 --> 00:00:54.375
<b>Here, Lord Krishna explains the inner </b>
<b>response of an enlightened soul.</b>

6
00:00:54.375 --> 00:00:57.625
<b>Such a person neither becomes </b>
<b>anxious in times of sorrow,</b>

7
00:00:57.625 --> 00:01:01.208
<b>nor gets overwhelmed with</b>
<b>joy in times of happiness.</b>

8
00:01:01.208 --> 00:01:08.708
<b>One who has conquered attachment, fear, </b>
<b>and anger such a person is called a sage.</b>

9
00:01:13.666 --> 00:01:19.750
<b>An ordinary person reacts intensely to suffering</b>

10
00:01:19.750 --> 00:01:21.166
<b>with agitation,</b>

11
00:01:21.166 --> 00:01:22.208
<b>worry,</b>

12
00:01:22.208 --> 00:01:23.291
<b>anger,</b>

13
00:01:23.291 --> 00:01:24.166
<b>and fear.</b>

14
00:01:24.166 --> 00:01:29.375
<b>But an enlightened soul remains </b>
<b>unmoved in such situations.</b>

15
00:01:29.375 --> 00:01:34.833
<b>Their mind stays peaceful even</b>
<b>in life's greatest challenges.</b>

16
00:01:34.833 --> 00:01:37.833
<b>They simply continue performing their duties.</b>

17
00:01:37.833 --> 00:01:39.000
<b>Similarly,</b>

18
00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:40.333
<b>when happiness comes,</b>

19
00:01:40.333 --> 00:01:45.125
<b>an enlightened person doesn't </b>
<b>become attached to that joy.</b>

20
00:01:45.125 --> 00:01:48.208
<b>They don't crave for more pleasure.</b>

21
00:01:48.208 --> 00:01:53.625
<b>Such a person maintains equanimity </b>
<b>in both joy and sorrow.</b>

22
00:01:53.625 --> 00:01:54.875
<b>Now, consider this</b>

23
00:01:54.875 --> 00:01:58.000
<b>where do happiness and sorrow come from?</b>

24
00:01:58.000 --> 00:01:59.541
<b>From desires.</b>

25
00:01:59.541 --> 00:02:03.166
<b>When things happen according </b>
<b>to our wishes, we feel happy;</b>

26
00:02:03.166 --> 00:02:05.750
<b>when they don't, we feel sorrow.</b>

27
00:02:05.750 --> 00:02:08.083
<b>But as we learned in the previous verse,</b>

28
00:02:08.083 --> 00:02:12.750
<b>an enlightened person has </b>
<b>already renounced their desires.</b>

29
00:02:12.750 --> 00:02:16.833
<b>So when there are no desires, </b>
<b>what basis remains for happiness or sorrow?</b>

30
00:02:16.833 --> 00:02:18.875
<b>This is worth contemplating.</b>

31
00:02:18.875 --> 00:02:28.041
<b>Furthermore, understand how such a person </b>
<b>overcomes attachment, fear, and anger.</b>

32
00:02:28.041 --> 00:02:30.916
<b>Attachment begins with attraction.</b>

33
00:02:30.916 --> 00:02:33.458
<b>When something gives us pleasure, </b>

34
00:02:33.458 --> 00:02:37.375
<b>our mind wishes to repeat that pleasure.</b>

35
00:02:37.375 --> 00:02:44.583
<b>Gradually, we reach a state where we don't want </b>
<b>to be separated from that source of joy.</b>

36
00:02:44.583 --> 00:02:47.583
<b>This is attachment.</b>

37
00:02:47.583 --> 00:02:52.125
<b>From this springs fear </b>
<b>the fear of losing what we're attached to.</b>

38
00:02:52.125 --> 00:02:56.875
<b>And if we do lose it, anger arises.</b>

39
00:02:56.875 --> 00:02:59.625
<b>But all of this began with attachment</b>

40
00:02:59.625 --> 00:03:02.708
<b>the desire for constant pleasure.</b>

41
00:03:02.708 --> 00:03:04.708
<b>And here again,</b>

42
00:03:04.708 --> 00:03:08.833
<b>an enlightened soul, by mastering their desires,</b>

43
00:03:08.833 --> 00:03:14.000
<b>overcomes attachment, fear, and anger.</b>

44
00:03:18.833 --> 00:03:25.291
<b>How do most people react to life's events?</b>

45
00:03:25.291 --> 00:03:26.625
<b>Typically,</b>

46
00:03:26.625 --> 00:03:31.458
<b>when things go their way, they become elated.</b>

47
00:03:31.458 --> 00:03:37.875
<b>And when circumstances turn </b>
<b>unfavorable, they sink into despair.</b>

48
00:03:37.875 --> 00:03:40.833
<b>Here's the fundamental issue</b>

49
00:03:40.833 --> 00:03:44.416
<b>neither are these events under your control,</b>

50
00:03:44.416 --> 00:03:50.583
<b>nor does life change its course </b>
<b>based on your reactions.</b>

51
00:03:50.583 --> 00:03:52.500
<b>Consider this scenario</b>

52
00:03:52.500 --> 00:03:54.708
<b>then share your thoughts.</b>

53
00:03:54.708 --> 00:03:58.250
<b>Picture a sailor steering a boat.</b>

54
00:03:58.250 --> 00:04:03.583
<b>Sometimes a wave comes that helps him, </b>
<b>pushing him forward,</b>

55
00:04:03.583 --> 00:04:07.541
<b>while other times a wave pushes him backward.</b>

56
00:04:07.541 --> 00:04:11.458
<b>Some waves are gentle, making no impact at all.</b>

57
00:04:11.458 --> 00:04:17.333
<b>In this situation, what should the sailor do?</b>

58
00:04:17.333 --> 00:04:18.416
<b>First option</b>

59
00:04:18.416 --> 00:04:27.875
<b>Should he keep sailing while learning how to </b>
<b>use different waves to his advantage?</b>

60
00:04:27.875 --> 00:04:29.375
<b>Second option</b>

61
00:04:29.375 --> 00:04:35.625
<b>Should he keep fluctuating between excitement</b>
<b>and distress with each wave?</b>

62
00:04:35.625 --> 00:04:36.750
<b>Third option</b>

63
00:04:36.750 --> 00:04:41.000
<b>Should he give up sailing </b>
<b>altogether out of exhaustion?</b>

64
00:04:41.000 --> 00:04:43.250
<b>You already know</b>

65
00:04:43.250 --> 00:04:46.500
<b>that waves will keep coming and going,</b>

66
00:04:46.500 --> 00:04:50.750
<b>and you know the right approach.</b>

67
00:04:50.750 --> 00:04:56.708
<b>So apply this wisdom to the ocean of your life:</b>

68
00:04:56.708 --> 00:04:59.916
<b>High and low waves will continue to come;</b>

69
00:04:59.916 --> 00:05:03.708
<b>reacting to them serves no purpose</b>

70
00:05:03.708 --> 00:05:04.583
<b>But</b>

71
00:05:04.583 --> 00:05:12.708
<b>if you keep sailing forward, you'll surely</b>
<b>learn how to maintain your composure </b>

72
00:05:12.708 --> 00:05:20.833
<b>and how to use life's waves to your advantage</b>

73
00:05:20.833 --> 00:05:22.708
<b>Keep moving forward</b>

74
00:05:27.666 --> 00:05:31.041
<b>You must have witnessed situations</b>

75
00:05:31.041 --> 00:05:39.500
<b>where extreme tension develops between </b>
<b>family members, brothers, or friends.</b>

76
00:05:39.500 --> 00:05:42.291
<b>Sometimes it escalates to the point</b>

77
00:05:42.291 --> 00:05:52.541
<b>where people become eager to harm </b>
<b>each other physically and mentally.</b>

78
00:05:52.541 --> 00:05:55.916
<b>Why does this happen?</b>

79
00:05:55.916 --> 00:05:57.041
<b>Attachment,</b>

80
00:05:57.041 --> 00:05:58.333
<b>fear,</b>

81
00:05:58.333 --> 00:06:00.833
<b>and anger.</b>

82
00:06:00.833 --> 00:06:08.541
<b>When someone becomes excessively </b>
<b>attached to wealth, property, or any object,</b>

83
00:06:08.541 --> 00:06:13.250
<b>they become unwilling to share it.</b>

84
00:06:13.250 --> 00:06:18.583
<b>This intense level of attachment </b>
<b>is called deep desire.</b>

85
00:06:18.583 --> 00:06:19.875
<b>In such situations,</b>

86
00:06:19.875 --> 00:06:25.625
<b>they become disturbed by the</b>
<b>fear of losing what they possess.</b>

87
00:06:25.625 --> 00:06:29.041
<b>This gives birth to their fear.</b>

88
00:06:29.041 --> 00:06:32.583
<b>Once fear takes root in the mind,</b>

89
00:06:32.583 --> 00:06:40.458
<b>they begin to suspect that others </b>
<b>are eyeing their possessions.</b>

90
00:06:40.458 --> 00:06:44.750
<b>It starts as defensive behavior</b>

91
00:06:44.750 --> 00:06:49.791
<b>but quickly turns aggressive.</b>

92
00:06:49.791 --> 00:06:56.333
<b>Anger becomes a natural response </b>
<b>whenever that possession is mentioned.</b>

93
00:06:56.333 --> 00:07:02.083
<b>This is where everything begins to unravel.</b>

94
00:07:02.083 --> 00:07:05.541
<b>They forget these essential truths:</b>

95
00:07:05.541 --> 00:07:06.541
<b>Perhaps</b>

96
00:07:06.541 --> 00:07:08.916
<b>their attachment was misplaced.</b>

97
00:07:08.916 --> 00:07:11.333
<b>Their fear was meaningless.</b>

98
00:07:11.333 --> 00:07:18.250
<b>Their suspicion was unproven, </b>
<b>merely a creation of their mind.</b>

99
00:07:18.250 --> 00:07:20.875
<b>And their anger</b>

100
00:07:20.875 --> 00:07:26.208
<b>was completely unjustified.</b>

101
00:07:26.208 --> 00:07:27.875
<b>Good relationships</b>

102
00:07:27.875 --> 00:07:31.750
<b>can only be built on the</b>
<b>foundation of a stable mind.</b>

103
00:07:31.750 --> 00:07:35.750
<b>This stability comes from spiritual wisdom.</b>

104
00:07:35.750 --> 00:07:38.333
<b>Spirituality teaches us</b>

105
00:07:38.333 --> 00:07:47.583
<b>that any wealth, land, or possession </b>
<b>is not more important than your state of mind.</b>

106
00:07:47.583 --> 00:07:49.500
<b>Spiritual knowledge</b>

107
00:07:49.500 --> 00:07:55.291
<b>protects this most precious state of mind.</b>

108
00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:06.125
<b>When someone behaves </b>
<b>aggressively in the workplace,</b>

109
00:08:06.125 --> 00:08:14.666
<b>our typical reaction is to label them </b>
<b>as arrogant and extremely selfish.</b>

110
00:08:14.666 --> 00:08:15.666
<b>However,</b>

111
00:08:15.666 --> 00:08:17.916
<b>it's possible</b>

112
00:08:17.916 --> 00:08:24.208
<b>that this aggression stems from hidden fear.</b>

113
00:08:24.208 --> 00:08:27.083
<b>Perhaps a task is proving difficult,</b>

114
00:08:27.083 --> 00:08:32.333
<b>and someone else is waiting to snatch it away.</b>

115
00:08:32.333 --> 00:08:43.000
<b>Maybe a superior has given a warning, </b>
<b>and this person is the sole earner in their family.</b>

116
00:08:43.000 --> 00:08:46.250
<b>There are numerous possibilities</b>

117
00:08:46.250 --> 00:08:52.708
<b>why someone might become </b>
<b>defensive about their work </b>

118
00:08:52.708 --> 00:08:56.750
<b>and aggressive towards others.</b>

119
00:08:56.750 --> 00:09:01.125
<b>Anger is born from fear.</b>

120
00:09:01.125 --> 00:09:07.000
<b>When you witness such behavior,</b>
<b>don't jump to conclusions.</b>

121
00:09:07.000 --> 00:09:12.208
<b>Try to understand the situation better if possible.</b>

122
00:09:12.208 --> 00:09:17.666
<b>And simultaneously, keep</b>
<b>looking within yourself.</b>

123
00:09:17.666 --> 00:09:21.291
<b>Examine your own behavior. </b>
<b>Why do you act the way you do?</b>

124
00:09:21.291 --> 00:09:27.583
<b>If you sometimes become aggressive, </b>
<b>what's the reason?</b>

125
00:09:27.583 --> 00:09:37.500
<b>This self-reflection will help you reach the </b>
<b>root of your mental state and control it. </b>

126
00:09:37.500 --> 00:09:43.250
<b>Self-reflection is the first step</b>
<b>toward self-control.</b>

